      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is even more difficult than I thought, since there\u0027s a narrow window for events to get lost here if another thread posts an event after `k_event_wait` returns but before `k_event_clear` completes.\n\nThe event API doesn\u0027t seem to provide a way to do this correctly (the closest it gets is the `reset` parameter to `k_event_wait`, but that ignores any events that are set when you go to wait rather than returning them) so I think this should instead use a condition variable (`k_condvar`) to guard the bitset of pending events: that will allow code reading and clearing the events to block any concurrent modifications.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "efac4adf5d6ca0cd053f394441199888d553cc29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
